    {
      "id": "gathering",
      "title": "Harvesting",
      "summary": "Taking things out of the ground",
      "intro": "Everything the trades below are made from starts here.",
      "entries": [
        {
          "id": "harvesting",
          "title": "Harvesting",
          "summary": "Nodes, levels, and why you stopped",
          "body": "Resource nodes belong to the server, not to the scenery. It tells the client which objects on the map can be gathered, what each one yields and what level it needs, so a node you can see is a node the server knows about.\n\nClick a node to start. The server reports that harvesting has begun and reports again when it stops - because you moved, because your backpack filled, or because something interrupted you. The client never decides that you have stopped.",
          "facts": [
            [
              "Started by",
              "clicking a node the server has described"
            ],
            [
              "Stopped by",
              "moving, a full backpack, or the server"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "bags",
          "title": "Bags on the ground",
          "summary": "What is dropped, and who may take it",
          "body": "Anything dropped becomes a bag standing on the ground where it fell. Opening one asks the server to describe it; what comes back is its contents at that moment and nothing older.\n\nA bag is not yours. Another player standing over it sees the same bag and can take from it, and the server settles who got what."
        },
        {
          "id": "storage",
          "title": "Storage",
          "summary": "What a storage keeper holds for you",
          "body": "Storage is held by the server, one set of shelves per character, reachable from a storage keeper. Deposits and withdrawals are its decision; the window shows the shelves as they were when it last described them.\n\nCarrying capacity applies on the way out. A withdrawal that would overload you is refused, and the goods stay where they were."
        },
        {
          "id": "harvesting-todo",
          "title": "There is no page per resource",
          "summary": "TODO - not written yet",
          "sections": [
            {
              "title": "Not written yet",
              "kind": "prose",
              "text": "Harvesting has written pages about how gathering works, but not one page per resource. The server knows where a resource stands and what it yields; it does not record a harvest level, a respawn time or what the thing is used for afterwards."
            },
            {
              "title": "What it needs",
              "kind": "facts",
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Have",
                  "Resource placement and yields, server-side"
                ],
                [
                  "Need",
                  "Harvest level, respawn, and uses per resource"
                ],
                [
                  "Where",
                  "config/eloria/harvesting.txt"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ],
          "body": "TODO. Harvesting has written pages about how gathering works, but not one page per resource. The server knows where a resource stands and what it yields; it does not record a harvest level, a respawn time or what the thing is used for afterwards.",
          "facts": [
            [
              "Have",
              "Resource placement and yields, server-side"
            ],
            [
              "Need",
              "Harvest level, respawn, and uses per resource"
            ],
            [
              "Where",
              "config/eloria/harvesting.txt"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "commerce",
      "title": "Trade",
      "summary": "Dealing with players and with the exchange",
      "intro": "Two ways to move goods between people, both settled by the server.",
      "entries": [
        {
          "id": "trade",
          "title": "Trading and the exchange",
          "summary": "Direct trades and the Nymara Exchange",
          "body": "A direct trade is between two players, and both must accept before anything moves. The server owns every step; the window shows what it has confirmed.\n\nThe Nymara Exchange takes listings and holds both goods and proceeds in escrow until they are collected."
        },
        {
          "id": "prices",
          "title": "What a thing is worth",
          "summary": "There is no fixed price list",
          "body": "Nothing in this encyclopedia states a price. The client is not told one, and a made-up figure would be worse than none.\n\nWhat the pages below do state is what a thing costs to make: its materials, the level it wants, and the food it burns. That is the floor under any price, and it comes from the server's own recipe table."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "alchemy",
      "title": "Alchemy",
      "summary": "Essences, bars and raw materials",
      "intro": "Alchemy turns what is harvested into the essences and bars the other trades consume.",
      "generate": "recipes:alchemy",
      "entries": []
    },
    {
      "id": "manufacturing",
      "title": "Manufacturing",
      "summary": "Armour, weapons and metalwork",
      "intro": "Metal work. Armour is made in pieces - helm, torso, legs, boots and shield - and the same bars go into the weapons that beat them.",
      "generate": "recipes:manufacturing",
      "entries": []
    },
    {
      "id": "crafting",
      "title": "Crafting",
      "summary": "Rings, medallions and worked goods",
      "intro": "Crafting wants a mould more often than it wants a fire.",
      "generate": "recipes:crafting",
      "entries": []
    },
    {
      "id": "engineering",
      "title": "Engineering",
      "summary": "Devices, traps and tools",
      "intro": "Things that are built rather than forged.",
      "generate": "recipes:engineering",
      "entries": []
    },
    {
      "id": "potions",
      "title": "Potions",
      "summary": "Everything that fills a vial",
      "intro": "A potion is mixed once and drunk once. What it does is the server's to apply.",
      "generate": "recipes:potion",
      "entries": []
    },
    {
      "id": "tailoring",
      "title": "Tailoring",
      "summary": "Thread, cloth, dye and clothing",
      "intro": "The longest recipe list in the client, and the one that most often wants a book first.",
      "generate": "recipes:tailoring",
      "entries": []
    },
    {
      "id": "summoning",
      "title": "Summoning",
      "summary": "Calling a creature to your side",
      "intro": "A summoning is paid for in stones and flesh, and the creature that arrives is the server's, not yours.",
      "generate": "recipes:summoning",
      "entries": []
    },
    {
      "id": "spells",
      "title": "Magic",
      "summary": "Sigils, spells and the effects they leave",
      "intro": "Choose a spell family, targeting mode and Power 1â€“10. Higher power replaces separate greater spells.",
      "generate": "spells",
      "entries": [
        {
          "id": "magic",
          "title": "Casting and power",
          "summary": "One effect, ten power levels",
          "body": "Own every listed sigil, carry the reagents and choose a power your Magic level and nexus support. Higher power increases healing, damage, protection or duration and costs more ether and reagents. Heal and Poison have no separate Greater versions. The spell window can be searched and filtered by targeting mode."
        },
        {
          "id": "spell-targets",
          "title": "Self, Target, Allies and Burst",
          "summary": "Choose who receives a spell",
          "body": "A base name such as Heal affects you. Target selects one actor within 15 tiles; Bolt also means one target. Allies affects you and party or guild members within four tiles. Burst selects a location within 15 tiles and affects eligible actors within four tiles of it. Hostile spells respect party, guild and PK restrictions. Escape cancels target selection without spending resources."
        },
        {
          "id": "wards-and-damage",
          "title": "Damage, wards and Dispel",
          "summary": "Match protection to the damage type",
          "body": "Magic Bolt deals magic damage; Fire Bolt heat; Frost Bolt cold; Radiation Bolt radiation. Each has a Burst form and a matching ward. Elemental Ward combines heat, cold and radiation protection. Shield improves physical protection. Dispel removes poison, cripple, resistance reductions and drained stats. Magic Immunity temporarily blocks hostile spells."
        },
        {
          "id": "transmute",
          "title": "Transmute",
          "summary": "Selected inventory items become gold",
          "body": "Choose an inventory item and quantity. Review the required power and exact gold return before casting. Common items need Power 1, Uncommon 3, Rare 5, Epic 7 and Legendary 9. Their gold multipliers are 1, 2, 4, 8 and 16 times the item base transmutation value. Only the selected quantity is consumed. Gold Coins and quest items cannot be transmuted."
        },
        {
          "id": "recall-portals",
          "title": "Recall and portal destinations",
          "summary": "Higher power opens destination selection",
          "body": "Recall at Power 1â€“4 returns you to Four Gates. At Power 5â€“10 choose a map with a portal entrance and the entrance where you will arrive. Maps with several entrances list each location. Blink remains a short teleport to a walkable place within 15 tiles."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "books",
      "title": "Books",
      "summary": "What must be read before it can be made",
      "intro": "A book is read once. Until the server records that you have read it, the recipes it teaches are refused however high your level is.",
      "generate": "books",
      "entries": []
    },
    {
      "id": "maps",
      "title": "Maps",
      "summary": "The regions of Nymara",
      "intro": "Each region is its own map on the server. Crossing between them is a change of map, not a walk across a seam.",
      "generate": "maps",
      "entries": []
    },
    {
      "id": "commands",
      "title": "Commands",
      "entries": [
        {
          "id": "commands-todo",
          "title": "Chat commands",
          "summary": "TODO - not written yet",
          "sections": [
            {
              "title": "Not written yet",
              "kind": "prose",
              "text": "The server keeps a one-line description of every chat command and answers #help with it. That line is all there is: nothing records a command's syntax, what it costs, where it cannot be used, or what it does on success, so a page per command cannot be generated from anything yet."
            },
            {
              "title": "What it needs",
              "kind": "facts",
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Have",
                  "One help line per command, server-side"
                ],
                [
                  "Need",
