  "prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept\nAsset type: square seamless albedo-only source tile for a low-poly fantasy forest terrain material\nPrimary request: Create a reusable forest-floor moss ground albedo for shaded old-growth woodland clearings and humid jungle pockets.\nStyle/medium: muted painterly low-poly fantasy ground in the understated Eloria material style; broad readable color masses and modest surface detail.\nComposition/framing: flat orthographic square texture; evenly distributed soft ground variation; left-right and top-bottom edges must meet seamlessly when tiled, with no frame or focal patch.\nColor palette: deep moss green, olive, dark umber soil and a few subdued leaf-brown notes; keep saturation restrained.\nMaterials/textures: soft mottled woodland loam with irregular low-contrast moss patches, faint decomposed leaf matter and sparse small rootlike fibers integrated into the ground; no distinct leaf or plant silhouettes; 4 metre intended terrain repeat.\nLighting/mood: uniform neutral diffuse albedo only, no shaded canopy or light pools.\nConstraints: both-axis seamless tile; moderate detail that stays calm at gameplay distance; texture coloration only.\nAvoid: standalone plants, leaves as recognizable objects, flowers, twigs, roots crossing the surface, bright lime green, dense high-frequency noise, large centerpiece, lighting gradients, directional shadows, highlights, perspective, horizon, borders, frame, text, logo, watermark.",
  "intendedRole": "ground",
  "worldRepeat": "4 m",
  "roughnessScalarSuggestion": 0.97,
